eDNAFlow LCA standalone adaptation

This package adapts the Lowest Common Ancestor taxonomy-assignment component
from eDNAFlow by Mahsa Mousavi-Derazmahalleh and contributors:
https://github.com/mahsa-mousavi/eDNAFlow

Original publication: Mousavi-Derazmahalleh et al. (2021), eDNAFlow, an
automated, reproducible and scalable workflow for analysis of environmental
DNA sequences exploiting Nextflow and Singularity. Molecular Ecology Resources.
DOI: 10.1111/1755-0998.13356

Upstream files retained for provenance:
- upstream_runAssign_collapsedTaxonomy.py
- upstream_working_function.py

Changes: removed runtime NCBI downloads; made taxonomy an explicit input;
added a named CLI, validation, deterministic outputs, tests, Python packaging,
and a Galaxy wrapper; removed fixed intermediate paths and shell side effects.

The derivative package is GPL-3.0. No endorsement by the original authors is implied.
